---
import MainLayout from "../components/MainLayout.astro";

const name = "Ben Davies";
---

<MainLayout {name}>
  <div
    class="md:bg-base md:border-border container p-2 md:mx-auto md:my-4 md:max-w-240 md:border-[1px]"
  >
    <header>
      <p class="select-none" aria-hidden>
        <span class="text-cyan">bend@bend.nz:~$</span>
        <span class="text-green">whoami</span>
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl">Ben Davies</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 select-none" aria-hidden>
        <span class="text-cyan">bend@bend.nz:~$</span>
        <span class="text-green">groups</span>
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-lg">software-engineer musician tinkerer</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 select-none" aria-hidden>
        <span class="text-cyan">bend@bend.nz:~$</span>
        <span class="text-green">cat</span> .git-credentials
      </p>
      <p>bachelor-of-engineering:hons@canterbury.ac.nz</p>
      <p class="mt-4 select-none" aria-hidden>
        <span class="text-cyan">bend@bend.nz:~$</span>
        <span class="text-green">cat</span> bookmarks.md
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          - <a class="underline" href="https://github.com/Benjamin-Davies"
            >Benjamin-Davies</a
          > on GitHub
        </li>
        <li>
          - <a
            class="underline"
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/benjamin-davies-657234226"
            >Benjamin Davies</a
          > on LinkedIn
        </li>
        <li>
          - Email me at <a
            class="underline"
            href="mailto:bentendavies@gmail.com">bentendavies@gmail.com</a
          >
        </li>
      </ul>
    </header>
    <section>
      <p class="mt-4 select-none" aria-hidden>
        <span class="text-cyan">bend@bend.nz:~$</span>
        <span class="text-green">cd</span> experience/ &&
        <span class="text-green">jj</span> log
      </p>
      <h3 class="font-bold">
        <span aria-hidden>
          <span class="text-green">@&nbsp;</span>
          <span class="text-pink">wy</span><span class="text-text2">vyuqxt</span
          >
        </span>
        <span class="text-yellow">Allied Telesis Labs</span>
        <span class="text-cyan">Jan 2026 - present</span>
        <span class="text-pink">main</span>
      </h3>
      <p>
        <span aria-hidden>│&nbsp;</span>
        <span class="font-bold">
          Platform support for <a
            class="underline"
            href="https://www.alliedtelesis.com/nz/en/about/technology/alliedware-plus"
            >AlliedWare Plus</a
          >
          (embedded Linux, C)
        </span>
      </p>
      <h3>
        <span aria-hidden>
          │ ○&nbsp;
          <span class="text-pink font-bold">u</span><span class="text-text2"
            >wurqsqw</span
          >
        </span>
        <span class="text-yellow">University of Canterbury</span>
        <span class="text-cyan">Mar 2025 - Oct 2025</span>
        <span class="text-pink">final-year-project</span>
      </h3>
      <p>
        <span aria-hidden>│ │&nbsp;</span>
        ML Signal Processing for <a
          class="underline"
          href="https://doi.org/10.1109/APMC60911.2024.10867297"
          >Harmonic Radar</a
        >
        (Tensorflow, Rust)
      </p>
      <h3>
        <span aria-hidden><span class="text-light-blue">◆</span> │&nbsp;</span>
        <span class="text-pink font-bold">x</span><span class="text-text2"
          >wrvtxtv</span
        >
        <span class="text-yellow">Allied Telesis Labs</span>
        <span class="text-cyan">Nov 2024 - Feb 2025</span>
        <span class="text-pink">internship</span>
      </h3>
      <p>
        <span aria-hidden>├─╯&nbsp;</span> Automation for testing network switches
        (Django, Openflow)
      </p>
      <h3>
        <span aria-hidden>
          <span class="text-light-blue">◆&nbsp;</span>
          <span class="text-pink font-bold">ww</span><span class="text-text2"
            >rwxsqu</span
          >
        </span>
        <span class="text-yellow">University of Canterbury</span>
        <span class="text-cyan">Nov 2023 - Feb 2024</span>
      </h3>
      <p>
        <span aria-hidden>│&nbsp;</span>
        <a
          class="underline"
          href="https://web.archive.org/web/20240224013548/https://www.findapest.nz/"
          >Find-A-Pest</a
        > migration (Kubernetes, AWS)
      </p>
      <h3>
        <span aria-hidden>
          <span class="text-light-blue">◆&nbsp;</span>
          <span class="text-pink font-bold">z</span><span class="text-text2"
            >xrrvyqs</span
          >
        </span>
        <span class="text-yellow">University of Canterbury</span>
        <span class="text-cyan">Nov 2022 - Feb 2023</span>
      </h3>
      <p>
        <span aria-hidden>│&nbsp;</span>
        <a class="underline" href="https://bugz.ento.org.nz/">BUGZ</a> rewrite (C#,
        Angular)
      </p>
      <p>~</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <p class="mt-4 select-none" aria-hidden>
        <span class="text-cyan">bend@bend.nz:~/experience$</span>
        <span class="text-green">cd</span> ../awesome/ &&
        <span class="text-green">cat</span> README.md
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <span class="select-none" aria-hidden>- </span>
          <a
            class="underline"
            href="https://github.com/actix/actix?tab=readme-ov-file">Actix</a
          > is an actor framework for Rust. I think that actors are a nice abstraction
          for stateful asynchronous programs. They also lend themselves to fault tolerant
          architectures, but I haven't used them for that yet.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="select-none" aria-hidden>- </span>
          <a
            class="underline"
            href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Gecko"
            >Gecko</a
          > is one of the last remaining browser engines. I think monopolies are bad,
          so why not take a small step to reduce Chromium's market share.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="select-none" aria-hidden>- </span>
          <a class="underline" href="https://www.jj-vcs.dev/latest/">Jujutsu</a> is
          a Git-compatible VCS. I especially like how it allows me to just make my
          changes without having to worry too much about what branch I'm on. It also
          makes squashing and rebasing a breeze.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="select-none" aria-hidden>- </span>
          <a class="underline" href="https://github.com/Benjamin-Davies/nestor"
            >Nestor</a
          > is prototype C language server (made by me). It ignores a lot of the weirdness
          of C in exchange for working well with large projects, or at least that's
          the plan.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="select-none" aria-hidden>- </span>
          <a class="underline" href="https://oracle.github.io/opengrok/"
            >OpenGrok</a
          > is a source code search engine. I find it quite useful for searching large
          C codebases. Who would've thought that Oracle could make something I choose
          to use.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="select-none" aria-hidden>- </span>
          <a class="underline" href="https://zed.dev/">Zed</a> is a snappy modern
          code editor. I mostly use it for the responsiveness and the clean aesthetic,
          but they also have a bunch of collaboration and AI features.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <footer>
      <p class="mt-4 select-none" aria-hidden>
        <span class="text-cyan">bend@bend.nz:~/awesome$</span>
        <span class="text-green">cat</span> ~/.config/colors.cfg
      </p>
      <p>
        Colours from Catppuccin
        <span class="dark:hidden">Late</span>
        <span class="not-dark:hidden">Mocha</span>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 select-none" aria-hidden>
        <span class="text-cyan">bend@bend.nz:~/awesome$</span>
        <span class="text-green">exit</span>
      </p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</MainLayout>
